  "body": "**What happens**\n\nhaas.cps writes an F word with no decimal point. In mm, `ff()` writes every feed as a whole number: it returns `String(Math.round(v))` (assets/posts/haas.cps, function `ff`). In inch, `trimNum()` removes the point from a whole value, so 50.8 mm/min posts as `F2`.\n\nThe Haas goldens show it. For example, crates/app/tests/golden/nc/haas/arc_planes.nc, line 15:\n\n```\nG18 G3 X15. Y0. Z0. I-5. K0. F600\n```\n\n**Why it is wrong**\n\nOn a Haas mill, Setting 77 (Scale Integer F) sets how the control reads an F word that has no decimal point. Source: Haas Mill Operator's Manual 96-8000 rev V (January 2009), Settings, \"77 - Scale Integer F\". In mm at the DEFAULT value (.001), F1 is F.001, so F600 is 0.6 mm/min. At INTEGER, F600 is 600 mm/min. The manual says: \"It is recommended that programmers always use a decimal point.\"\n\nThe post cannot know Setting 77 on the machine. With a decimal point, the control reads the same feed at all values of Setting 77.\n\n#1836 fixed the same problem for the length words: `pt()` adds the point. `ff()` does not use `pt()`.\n\n**What should happen**\n\nEvery F word that haas.cps writes has a decimal point, for example `F600.`, `F23.62` and `F2.`.\n\n**Steps to reproduce**\n\n1. Post a mill operation in mm with the Haas post, or open crates/app/tests/golden/nc/haas/arc_planes.nc.\n2. Look at the F words. They are `F600`, not `F600.`.\n\nVersion: main 8c6b77f94 (v0.25.0-519). Linux.\n\n**Done means**\n\n- `ff()` always writes a decimal point, in mm and in inch.\n- The Haas goldens show `F600.` and the other feeds with a point.\n- A test fails when haas.cps writes an F word with no decimal point.\n\nNot checked: the other posts.\n\nFound while: we posted a 3-axis test part through haas.cps (CamCraft 0.25.0, machine haas-vf2ss.mch) for one of our Haas VF-2SS YT mills. All feeds had no decimal point.\n\nWe have a fix with two tests on our side. We can send it as a pull request.\n\n---\nAn agent (Claude Code) wrote and opened this issue for LiamJDL. This account cannot set labels. Suggested labels: `source:agent`, `bug`, `area:post`, `P1`, `effort:high`.\n",
